## Order of accuracy

In smooth regions away from interfaces and walls the scheme is second order
in space. In time, advection and forces are second order; the viscous term
(backward Euler) is first order. Near the interface the reconstruction is
first order in the position of the interface within a cell but second order
for the curvature from height functions. Limiters, the step function
$\chi$ and cut cells all reduce the local order. In practice, the accuracy
of a result is governed by how many cells resolve the features that matter,
and by the treatment of open boundaries, more than by the formal order.
Check it by running the same case at two or three levels.

